## Identity
- Year 2160, Io survival + light base-builder + **Lite Building** colony camp, semi-low-poly, **PC first + consoles**
- 25 companions max: **22 base camp** + **switchable trio of 3** on expeditions with the player
- Rescue procedural **Neural Echoes**; **Aether-9** memory cores → **Resonance Events**
- O₂ norm + radiation, thermal, volcanism, sulfur storms, **alien life forms**, **AI androids**
- Materialize/craft/maintain buildings + **attachment modules** (generators, power grids, auto gather, logistics, communications, defense, mining)
- **Runtime:** **The World Engine** (WoOS) — World → Simulation → Intelligence → Experience → Presentation → Player

## Locked decisions (do not contradict)
- **Platforms:** PC (primary) + consoles (PS5 / Xbox) only. No mobile-as-target.
- **Economy:** **Aether Credits (AC) only**. Starter **5000 AC** → pick **1 starter Skilled Companion**. Spend at **vendors**. No external wallet, marketplace mint, or third-party crypto loop.
- **Echo / roster trading:** local save progression only — no marketplace trading of Echoes.
- **Thermal:** single **cold/heat** meter (one bar, two poles)
- **Pet:** fold legacy pet/AI follower into **Echo/trio** system — no separate pet loop (migration still outstanding in prototype)
- **Base 22:** impervious to most pressures; **sulfur storms** → Command Center rooms; building damage **injures, never kills**
- **Classes:** Architect Engineer, Science Specialist, Combat Tactician, Infiltrator Scout, Med Tech, Logistics Officer, Salvage Engineer (+ hybrids)
- **Building Control Panels:** each major structure has an in-world terminal (E) → **Building Control UI** with tabs **Overview | Companions | Production | Craft | Changes**. Assign base-22 companions, queues, and per-building / module settings here. Planned attachment modules: generators, power grids, automated gather/logistics, communications, defense, mining. **Journal Craft = recipe library / scroll learning only** — not primary production UI. Queues pause in sulfur storms.

## Before building off-design
If the user asks for features unrelated to the GDD, **ask** whether it is canon, prototype, or a new direction. Prototypes OK when explicitly labeled.

## Unity scope
- Code lives under `Assets/_Project/`
- Reuse existing systems (combat, inventory, quests, save) where possible
- Prototype is flat terrain — Io biomes not shipped yet
- Prefer **Aether Credits** for all economy UI/save; strip leftover legacy currency naming when touching those systems
- Check GDD 5.0 **Appendix B** before assuming a vision system is missing or already shipped

